l2 ssmis files contain:
#       double longitude(nobs) ;
#       double latitude(nobs) ;
#       int quality(nobs) ;
#       float land_flag(nobs) ;
#       int dtg_yyyymmdd(nobs) ;
#       int dtg_hhmm(nobs) ;
As well as 
tb_19V
tb_19H
tb_22V
tb_37V
tb_37H
tb_92V
tb_92H
tb_150H
ice_concentration

Note that stacker may train input classifiers/regressors or they may be 
  trained separately and passed to stacker

classifier -- limited set of integers
regressor  -- regress on continuum values


sklearn Classifiers:
from sklearn.ensemble  import StackingClassifier
from sklearn.ensemble  import RandomForestClassifier
from sklearn.ensemble  import GradientBoostingClassifier
from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier
from sklearn.tree      import DecisionTreeClassifier
from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression
from sklearn.svm       import SVC                   -- slowest by far

sklearn Regressors:
from sklearn.ensemble     import StackingRegressor
from sklearn.ensemble     import RandomForestRegressor
from sklearn.tree         import DecisionTreeRegressor
from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression
from sklearn.linear_model import Lasso

#----------------------------------------------------------------

build and save a stacking classifier      --   classify.py
read in and use a stacking classifier     --   reclassify.py
build and save individual classifiers as well as stacker --  class2.py
build a classifier and then a regressor on what classifier says is ice -- class_regress.py

Train and save a regressor                --  regressing.py
Run a pre-trained random forest regressor --  reregr.py

Timing the classifiers                    --  time_class.py

Filter input Tb to be at least some distance from each other -- distance.py

